implementationPlan.description:
Test fixtures.

(a) NEW scripts/tests/postflight-fake-agent-seat.js: the agent-seat stub that MOE_AGENT_SEAT_PATH names. It is CommonJS like postflight-fake-proxy.js, with the same style of header, and is shared so CQ-M07m and the ps1 twin (CQ-M07n) can reuse it.
- Its argv is exactly the real CLI's (`<cmd> --project <abs> ...`).
- Every call appends ONE row {tool:'agent-seat', args:{cmd, argv, env: process.env, ...}} to <project>/.moe/evidence-rpcs.jsonl, the fake proxy's RPC log. Rows can then order seat calls against claim_next_task and deregister_worker in one file.
- seat-start: answers {ok:true, instance, executionReady:false} and exits 0. The instance is moe-vm-<20 hex from a per-project counter>, so each start gets a new one.
- seat-job:
  - reads stdin to EOF and records only {stdinName, stdinSha256}, never the value;
  - FAKE_SEAT_JOB_SLEEP=<s> makes it sleep after recording (for the Ctrl+C row);
  - worker: builds the admitted tree in --checkout with plumbing on a private GIT_INDEX_FILE (read-tree the commit, hash-object -w a vm-job.txt blob, update-index --add --cacheinfo, write-tree), and records the tree;
  - prints one line of job output to stdout and one to stderr;
  - then prints the outcome line in CQ-M07j's landed shape (read agent-seat.mjs): {seatJob:1, ok:true, role, commit, baseTree, tree, digest, paths:[{path:'vm-job.txt', kind:'file'}], exitCode:0, signal:null, lease, executionReady:false};
  - qa: the same, with tree == baseTree and paths [];
  - exits 0.
- seat-stop: answers {ok:true, instance, vm: as CQ-M07i answers} and exits 0.
- Keep the answers knob-driven, so CQ-M07m can add exit-75 and failure answers without restructuring.

(b) scripts/tests/postflight-fake-proxy.js: FAKE_CTX_LANDING (JSON) becomes get_context's task.landing. Document it at its handler, beside FAKE_CTX_WORKSPACE. The QA row reads lastCompletion.sha from it.
